{title: What a Friend We Have in Jesus}
{lyricist: Joseph M. Scriven}
{composer: Charles C. Converse}
{year: 1855}
{meta: tune-year 1868}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{meta: tune CONVERSE}
{meta: meter 8.7.8.7 D}
{meta: variation The hymn, sung to CONVERSE}
{meta: license public-domain}
{meta: tags prayer, comfort}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]What a friend we [C]have in [G]Jesus,
[G]All our sins and [A7]griefs to [D]bear!
[G]What a privi[C]lege to [G]carry
[G]Everything to [D]God in [G]prayer!
[D]O what peace we [G]often forfeit,
[D]O what needless [G]pain we [A7]bear, [D]
[G]All because we [C]do not [G]carry
[G]Everything to [D]God in [G]prayer!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Have we trials [C]and temp[G]tations?
[G]Is there trouble [A7]any[D]where?
[G]We should never [C]be dis[G]couraged;
[G]Take it to the [D]Lord in [G]prayer.
[D]Can we find a [G]friend so faithful
[D]Who will all our [G]sorrows [A7]share? [D]
[G]Jesus knows our [C]every [G]weakness;
[G]Take it to the [D]Lord in [G]prayer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Are we weak and [C]heavy [G]laden,
[G]Cumbered with a [A7]load of [D]care?
[G]Precious Savior, [C]still our [G]refuge;
[G]Take it to the [D]Lord in [G]prayer.
[D]Do thy friends de[G]spise, forsake thee?
[D]Take it to the [G]Lord in [A7]prayer! [D]
[G]In His arms He'll [C]take and [G]shield thee;
[G]Thou wilt find a [D]solace [G]there.
{end_of_verse}
